          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "In 1953, Roth proved that every subset of the integers of positive upper density contains a nontrivial three-term arithmetic progression. This can be stated in the following finite form. ::: theorem []{#thm:roth label=\"thm:roth\"} For every $\\alpha>0$, if $N$ is sufficiently large, then every set $A\\subset\\{0,1,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ with $\\lvert A\\rvert\\geq\\alpha N$ contains a three-term arithmetic progression",
      "extractCut": true
    },
