          "term": "sum",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "Write $[N]=\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ and choose a prime $m$ with $4N<m<8N$, which we may do by Bertrand's postulate. We embed $[N]$ in $\\mathbb{Z}_m$ in the obvious way. The point of choosing $m>2N$ is that a three-term progression in $\\mathbb{Z}_m$ whose terms all lie in $[N]$ is a genuine integer progression. Let $\\alpha=\\lvert A\\rvert/N$ be the density of $A$ in $[N]$, and define $f=\\mathbf{1}_A-\\alpha\\mathbf{1}_{[N]}$",
      "extractCut": true
    },
