      "extract": "Our next goal is to find a long modular progression on which $f$ has positive average. For an integer $1\\leq \\ell<m/2$ and a step $d\\in\\mathbb{Z}_m$, set $$S_d(x):=\\sum_{i=0}^{\\ell-1}f(x+id),\\qquad V_d:=\\sum_{x\\in\\mathbb{Z}_m}\\lvert S_d(x)\\rvert^2.$$ Thus $S_d(x)$ is the sum of $f$ on the length-$\\ell$ modular progression starting at $x$ with step $d$, and $V_d$ is the second moment of these sums as $x$ varies. :::",
